      "id": "sec-cp-14",
      "type": "reflection",
      "body": "The tragedy of modern life is not that we run out of time; it is that we operate under the delusion that time is something we possess, rather than something that possesses us. We hoard our hours for the people who demand them with invoices and deadlines, and we steal them from the people who love us enough to wait. And when the waiting finally ends, we find ourselves holding clean spreadsheets, immaculate audit trails, and an empty chair on a verandah where we will sit alone for the rest of our lives."
